  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Initiating UI Foundation**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in \"Etapa 1,\" focusing intently on the UI Foundation and Navigation elements for the \"Nisti Work\" application. The architecture has been refined and given the green light, and so I am progressing. I\'m focusing on user interface aspects.\n\n\n**Defining Frontend Structure**\n\nI\'ve outlined ten key constraints and decisions, including UUIDs, SKU uniqueness, and UTC date handling. I\'m prioritizing the frontend foundation now, generating the React structure, Tailwind styling, and essential UI elements like a sidebar, routing, and empty pages. The architecture is becoming focused, and I\'m pushing for a dark theme integration.\n\n\n**Implementing Frontend Structure**\n\nI\'m now deep-diving into the practical implementation. The focus is now on crafting the file structure and defining the UI, as well as installing dependencies like `react-router-dom`, `clsx`, and `tailwind-merge`. I am configuring Tailwind for a dark mode with modern colors, and I\'ve detailed the folder structure, including UI components, pages, types (enums, interfaces), and utilities. My focus remains on the dashboard\'s immediate needs, and I\'m validating the layout with mock data.\n\n\n**Constructing Initial Components**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the practical steps of my plan. I\'ve focused on installing the necessary dependencies such as react-router-dom, clsx, and tailwind-merge. I\'m busy crafting core types, date utilities, and standard Tailwind configurations to support a dark, professional, and spacious theme. Next, I\'ll be creating the foundational UI components and mocked pages and routing to support the dashboard\'s needs. I\'m drafting the code for types, including UUID string types, and also the Priority enum.\n\n\n**Developing Core Components**\n\nI\'m now implementing the core components. I\'m focusing on defining crucial enums like Priority and Status for tasks, companies, etc., alongside base entities. The date utilities (formatToLocal, formatToISO) are crucial and I\'ve set up dark mode variables in CSS with Tailwind\'s zinc or slate. I\'m creating the `Layout`, `Sidebar`, `Badge`, and `Card` components, ready for the initial pages: Dashboard, Queue, Companies, Production, Collections, Products, and Settings, all wired up in App.tsx.\n\n\n**Enhancing UI Layout**\n\nI\'m now zeroed in on optimizing the visual framework. I\'m leveraging `h-screen` for a full-height desktop app, with a fixed-width sidebar and `flex-1 overflow-y-auto` for the main content. The dark theme is now refined to `bg-zinc-950 text-zinc-50` for the body, and a `bg-zinc-900 border-r border-zinc-800` for the sidebar, alongside clean typography choices. I\'m executing the plan with new tool calls. I\'m creating the final output, and reviewing it to match the constraints.\n\n\n"
